# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only material. Everything below stays on the machine that produced it:
# the corpora, the experiments behind the shipped dictionary, and the scratch
# tooling. Only the package itself (autobm25/, rust/, setup.py, READMEs) is
# meant to reach a clone or a wheel.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Datasets (BEIR downloads, subsamples, language splits) - fetched, never shipped
dataset/
dataset_en/
dataset_cn/
datasets/

# Research pipeline output: benchmark tables, grid searches, mixes, documents
results/
research/
document/

# Local tooling and scratch directories (bench harnesses, downloaded installers)
_bench/
_tools/
_scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python build artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust build output and the compiled Python extension.
#
# `rust/` itself is deliberately *tracked*: the sources are what let a user
# compile the accelerator on their own machine (`python rust/build_pyext.py`).
# Only the artefacts are ignored - `rust/target/` is cargo's scratch directory
# and the compiled extension is rebuilt by `pip install .` / `pip wheel .`
# (see setup.py), so a stale binary can never be committed by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rust/target/
*.pyd
*.so
*.dylib
